the delta variant is a mutated variant  of the original coronavirus and was  first identified in india in december  2020 leading to major outbreaks in the  country it then spread rapidly and is  now reported in over a hundred countries  across the world the delta variant also  known as b16172  can spread more easily according to  health officials  the strain has mutations on the spike  protein that make it easier for it to  infect human cells that means people may  be more contagious if they contract the  virus and more easily spread it to  others it is now the dominant strain in  many parts of the world including the uk  and the united states according to  estimates the delta variant is between  50 and 60 more contagious as previous  versions of the virus researchers are  still trying to understand the mutations  that account for this but preliminary  studies suggest that changes in its  spike protein make it more efficient at  both grabbing onto receptors and getting  into your cells  the delta variant also seems to lead to  higher viral loads than other variants  viral load is a measure of how much  virus is in your nose and throat one  study found that at the beginning of  their infection people with the delta  variant had viral loads a thousand times  greater than those people infected with  the original version of the virus people  with delta variant also reach their peak  viral load faster according to this  study which has not yet gone through  peer review the delta variant poses a  threat to us all not just those  countries with large numbers of  unvaccinated people this is because  unlike the previous alpha variant which  first emerged in the uk  the first doses of the vaccines do not  offer enough protection against it  meaning people are at risk in the  interval period between the two doses  according to public health england a  study they published in may a single  dose of either astrazeneca or pfizer's  vaccine only reduces a person's risk of  developing covid19 symptoms caused by  the delta variant by 33  a second dose of the astrozenica vaccine  boosts protection against delta to 60  while two doses of pfizer protect up to  88  the delta plus variant also known as  b161721  is considered a sub variant of the delta  version it has a mutation that allows  the virus to better attack lung cells  and potentially escape vaccines  first identified in india delta plus has  now been found in the us uk and nearly a  dozen of other countries  india has labelled it a varied concern  but the who haven't  the key to protection is to get fully  vaccinated it is only by taking both  doses of the vaccine can you protect  yourself against serious illness from  the delta variants  you
 

